  "draft_markdown": "## MA-S3: Query Expansion and Loss Reduction\n\nThis section details the implementation of the dedicated attention model, focusing on tensor shape manipulation, conditional positional encoding, and loss computation.\n\n### 1. Query Reshaping\nThe query tensor is reshaped to include a new dimension for the attention mechanism. The operation `query = query.unsqueeze(1)  # [batch_size, 1, hidden_size]` transforms the query into a shape suitable for subsequent concatenation.\n\n### 2. Configuration Loading\nThe model configuration is accessed to determine whether positional encoding should be applied. The check `if self.cfg.add_positional_encoding:` loads the configuration value to control the execution flow.\n\n### 3. Conditional Positional Encoding\nIf the condition `self.cfg.add_positional_encoding` is true, the model computes and adds positional embeddings to the passages. This branch is conditional and depends on the configuration state:\n\n```\nif self.cfg.add_positional_encoding:\n            # document_id might be out of range, so we need to modulate it and plus the quotient\n            document_id_embeddings = self.document_id_embedding(\n                (document_id.long() % self.cfg.retrieval.top_k)\n                + (document_id.long() // self.cfg.retrieval.top_k)\n            )  # [batch_size, num_passages, hidden_size]\n            passage_id_embeddings = self.passage_id_embedding(\n                passage_id.long()\n            )  # [batch_size, num_passages, hidden_size]\n            # Directly add the positional encoding to the passages\n            passages = (\n                passages + document_id_embeddings + passage_id_embeddings\n            )  # [batch_size, num_passages, hidden_size]\n```\n\nWithin this branch, the document ID embeddings are computed via `document_id_embeddings = self.document_id_embedding(`. The specific calculation involves modulating the document ID to handle out-of-range values, as shown in `document_id_embeddings = self.document_id_embedding(\n                (document_id.long() % self.cfg.retrieval.top_k)\n                + (document_id.long() // self.cfg.retrieval.top_k)\n            )  # [batch_size, num_passages, hidden_size]`.\n\n### 4. Embedding Concatenation\nAfter processing the passages, the query and passages are concatenated along the sequence dimension. The operation `concat_embeddings = torch.cat(\n            (query, passages), dim=1\n        )  # [batch_size, num_passages + 1, hidden_size]` produces the final input for the attention mechanism.\n\n### 5. Loss Reduction\nThe final loss is computed by averaging the stacked losses. The reduction operation `loss = torch.stack(losses).mean()` aggregates the individual loss values into a single scalar loss for backpropagation.",
